From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Weber <doweb85@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:34:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] byteplan: expert map across all GPU cores, MoE tiles
 skip empty 8-token rows

kernel_mul_mm_id_map0 ran as one threadgroup scanning every token on one GPU core; it now counts each expert's rows per
chunk of 32 tokens (map0_cnt) and writes them after the rows of the earlier chunks, one threadgroup per chunk - the same
lists in the same order. kernel_mul_mm_id gives each simdgroup 8 token rows of the tile (all 64 weight rows), so a
simdgroup without rows of the expert skips its MMAs; each output element sees the same MMA sequence as before.
test-backend-ops: qwen4exp expert and QSA attention perf shapes, a QSA-budget sparse attention test.
